          { name: "Assuming Anglo Homeowner Coalition Stability", tag: "avoid", why: "While the 62.9% white population and (inferred) higher homeownership rate provide the base for Mannix's 52%, this coalition is only secure if the economic concerns of the working-class, non-college-educated majority (76.1% without college degrees) are being addressed. Oregon's economic pressures affect homeowners as well as renters — property tax, inflation, wage stagnation — and messaging that takes for granted that homeowners will vote Republican regardless of whether government is delivering for them will leave this constituency open to a challenger who offers credible economic remedies." }
