          "Treat the 52-48 result as evidence of a genuinely competitive seat, not a comfortable hold: a 4-point margin with a 28% Hispanic population and 44.7% renter rate is one strong Democratic turnout operation or one credible challenger away from flipping, and any incumbent who campaigns this seat with the confidence of a 55%+ winner is strategically blind to its actual vulnerability."
