          { name: "Treating the Unopposed Result as Stable Electoral Reality", tag: "avoid", why: "A 100% result in 2024 reflects a lack of opposition, not necessarily dominant support — and in a district with 35.2% Hispanic plurality, 32% renters, and $66,489 median income, the absence of Democratic organization is a structural vulnerability rather than evidence of Republican strength. Any incumbent who campaigns as though this margin is durable, rather than as though opposition is simply unorganized, risks being blindsided by a challenger who invests in the constituent relationship infrastructure that an unopposed cycle allows to atrophy. The strategic fact is not that Republicans dominate OR-HD-57 but that Democrats have not yet competed for it." }
