          "Mobilize the renter constituency: 32% of households rent, meaning one-third of OR-HD-57 does not benefit from homeowner-oriented policy and faces direct housing-cost pressure; housing affordability, renter protections, and anti-displacement policy offer direct material appeals to this demographic.",
          "Treat the unopposed result as opportunity, not barrier: the absence of Democratic opposition in 2024 created a structural vacuum in constituent service and political engagement; any challenger who invests in filling that vacuum—before the election cycle formally begins—can establish credible legitimacy as an alternative in a district that has never been genuinely contested."
